WEBVTT

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.890
I'll send letters.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.960
Me, too.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.720
I made these.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.390
They're so cute!

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:32.590
They're a pair.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:34.340
Will you take one?

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.550
Yeah!

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.100
Thanks!

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.590
Hey, what are their names?

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:44.100
Their names? I didn't think of that...

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.000
You name them, Suzu.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.860
Then... Riru and Meru.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.530
Okay! That's cute!

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.900
Riru and...

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:53.950
Meru!

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.290
Thank you.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:03.450
I'll take good care of it.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.540
We'll be friends forever!

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:09.040
Yeah, no matter what happens!

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.210
We'll be together forever!

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:20.890
Hey, Dad, over there...

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:22.600
Oh, right at the next corner.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.580
<i>I'm back.</i>

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.750
<i>Back in this town.</i>

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Memories / Front and Back

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.590
<b>Homura</b>

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:54.920
Okay, okay...

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.420
All right, stop.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.010
Okay, this goes there.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:05.270
Here?

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:06.550
That's right.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:09.110
Um, I'll help.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:10.890
It's all right.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.480
Everything is included in the fee.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.300
There we go!

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.260
Morning!

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.760
<b>Dinner Money</b>

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.480
Okay, sit down!

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.940
I'll introduce the new transfer student.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:03:05.410
<b>Homura Suzuko</b>

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.630
Homura Suzuko-san.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:03:00.100
She's transferred from Hokkaido to our 
second-year class for family reasons.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.950
Introduce yourself.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.920
O-Okay.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.410
I'm Homura Suzuko.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:09.210
I lived here until my second 
year of elementary school.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.040
And now I've come back.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.950
Please be friends with me.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.880
Thank you very much.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.840
All right, homeroom is over.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.860
First period is science.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.130
Science Room #2. Hurry.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.800
Okay.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.140
Science Room #2, huh?

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.490
Wait a second!

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:28.470
Um...

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.440
Where is Science Room #2?

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.240
Go up the central stairs, and it's on the left.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.170
Um, would you show me—

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:36.940
What are you doing?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.460
Hurry!

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.210
Sorry!

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.430
What were you talking about?

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:43.240
She just asked where the science room is.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.740
<b>Daily Veggies</b>

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.060
This deck is amazing!

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:52.850
Right?

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:55.460
If you think I'm the same girl as yesterday, 
you're in for a big surprise!

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.390
Okay, here I go.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.420
I'll hit your LRIG directly!

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.220
Wait!

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.170
Attack Phase. I'll defend with Coating Fan!

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:06.560
Seriously? I lose.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.970
I'm hitting the card shop on my way home.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.970
Deck... LRIG?

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.270
Card shop?

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.020
All right!

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.080
<b>From: Dad 
To: Suzuko 
No Subject 

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.350
What should I do?

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.040
I made too much.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.040
<b>Please warm and eat it.</b>

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.420
<b>Homura Suzuko</b>

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.420
I remember all of these.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:48.100
<b>Recipient Not At This Address 

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.100
<b>Recipient Not At This Address</b>

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:56.180
Turn at the corner with the 
white condo building...

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:57.900
Here!

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.450
<b>Fujihara</b>

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:09.910
Do you need something?

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.020
Excuse me.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.580
Do you know where the Morikawa family

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.370
who lived here until about 
three years ago went?

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:21.160
I'm afraid I don't...

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.210
I'm sorry.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.710
I see.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.020
Sorry to bother you.

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.620
You can do it, Suzu!

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.350
I know you can do it.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.150
Let's give it one more try!

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.150
Up, and...

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.150
See? You did it!

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:48.740
Yeah, I did it!

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.980
I did it!

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.370
I didn't realize it was so low.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.660
Let's do the iron bar next!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.860
I can't do it...

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:58.810
It's fine.

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:00.160
You do it like this.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.950
<i>Where are you, Chi-chan?</i>

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:03.840
Welcome. Will you be eating here?

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.130
Here you go.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.090
This is your cheeseburger combo.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.430
<b>Morikawa</b>

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.090
Enjoy.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.470
You bought another new pack?

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.390
I wanted to strengthen my deck.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.350
WIXOSS is so addictive.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.740
You should enter a tournament.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.310
Yeah.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:21.520
I'm back.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:22.500
Welcome home.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:23.390
Welcome home.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:26.200
I'll have some dinner, too, Mom.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.040
Oh, dear...

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.570
You didn't eat before you came home?

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:31.270
No, the store was crowded today.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.320
Going in on a Saturday...

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:35.280
Sure you aren't working too much?

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:37.040
Lately, they've really depended on me.

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:40.130
But it means I get paid more per hour.

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:41.650
Sorry about this...

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:44.020
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.120
Oh, come on, Dad!

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.920
I'm doing this job because I like it.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.320
And I'm keeping up with my studies, too.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:52.390
It's fine.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:10.900
Hey, that transfer student...

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.060
Oh, Homura-san.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.090
Did you see her bag?

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:14.930
I did. What's that little mascot on her bag?

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.080
It looks handmade.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.560
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.410
It looks like something an elementary 
school kid would choose.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:24.270
And it's kind of dirty, too.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:27.330
Stop it. I feel bad for her.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:29.550
It was probably popular at her school.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:30.420
In the country?

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.030
Deep in the mountains, in the country.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.740
You're meaner than I am!

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:48.190
<b>We Buy and Sell</b>

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:48.190
A card shop, huh?

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.900
If I learned to play, could I play with everyone?

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.390
Was that Homura-san?

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:56.830
Yeah.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:00.800
SIGNI... Spells.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.790
<b>Flow of the Game</b>

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:01.790
ARTS.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:05.680
There are so many!

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:06.910
What's this?

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.340
LRIG...

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:15.300
So pretty.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:23.110
Welcome! Welcome! Welcome!

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:25.780
Welcome, Selector! Welcome...

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.360
Welcome, Selector.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.320
I am the LRIG of the beginning.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.200
What?

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:41.700
I shall register your memories.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.700
Welcome, Selector.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:16.910
Where am I?

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:18.870
Who are you?

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.540
Welcome, Selector.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.750
Selector? Me?

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:30.390
I am a LRIG.

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:31.710
Give me a name.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:33.760
A name?

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:36.500
You name them, Suzu.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:41.020
R-Riru...

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:43.240
The same name as that mascot, yes?

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:43.720
Eh?

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.120
How did you know?

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:53.300
Because I am part of you.

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:58.600
Another part of me?

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:04.760
These are your memories, Suzuko.

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:09.100
Humans are made of memories 
that comprise their past.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:12.210
In other words, these coins are you.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:15.960
Cards...

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:18.160
Choose one.

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:22.810
Th-This one.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.560
Entry completed.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:33.980
You will be given one coin, 
and the battle will begin.

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.290
What do you mean by "battle"?

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:41.870
For the next ninety days,

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:45.790
you will participate in a Selector 
battle among chosen

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:48.040
who have been given a LRIG.

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:50.720
I don't know anything about that.

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:52.670
I've never been in a battle!

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.060
I can't do that!

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:55.870
You cannot refuse to fight.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:00.380
If you win, one black coin will turn gold.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:03.260
If you lose, one gold coin will turn black.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.470
If all five coins turn gold,

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:09.020
you will retake who you are.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:11.480
And you can leave the battles behind.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:12.480
And...

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:18.240
If all five turn black, you will disappear.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:21.910
That is a Selector battle.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:28.750
Ener Charge! Attack!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.500
Seriously?

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.780
Is this over?

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:32.460
Idiot.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:33.540
It's just beginning.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.250
Not ready to give up?

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:37.020
Want to play?

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.550
You went to the card shop yesterday, right?

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:41.760
Hey, let's fight a battle!

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:43.720
S-Sorry...

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:46.430
I don't know the rules very well.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:48.070
I'm really sorry.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:54.010
Why don't you battle?

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.770
They aren't Selectors.

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:03.360
If you get practice in the regular game,

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.860
it will help you in the real battles.

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:07.590
It doesn't matter...

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:10.230
I'm not doing any battles.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.670
I told you that you cannot refuse.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.180
Why?

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:16.550
Why me?

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:17.520
Because you were chosen.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:18.810
That's so selfish!

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:20.840
I never wanted to be chosen—

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.670
It doesn't matter. You were chosen.

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:24.590
<b>Homura Suzuko</b>

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:24.590
That is all.

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:26.230
No...

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:28.660
You said if I lose one time, I'll disappear.

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:31.060
So how can I fight a battle?

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:33.810
If you don't fight, the result will be the same.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.300
The coins have a time limit on them.

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:40.600
If you do nothing, they will eventually disappear.

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:43.010
Win the battles.

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:46.140
You have no other choice.

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:47.310
That's...

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:51.090
Even as we speak, your memories 
are being devoured—

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:53.540
A Selector is coming!

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.870
Down the stairs! She's close!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:57.750
Blindness.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:01.340
I didn't expect you to attend the same school.

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:02.670
U-Um...

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:03.840
Fight.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:04.840
Hi!

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:08.520
I-I'm not doing it...

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:09.920
I'm not doing any battles.

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:10.680
Inexplicable.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.460
You aren't a Selector?

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:14.640
I-I'm...

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:17.980
I'm sorry!

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:24.440
Why?

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:27.910
Why am I a Selector?

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:29.600
I can't fight any battles.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:32.130
I can't fight...

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:34.060
You won't fight alone.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:38.080
I am a part of you.

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.050
<b>Dinner Money</b>

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:48.160
Good morning.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:58.840
Suzuko.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.230
What?

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.360
Are you really not going to fight?

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:04.310
No.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:06.440
Look at the coins.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:07.980
The coins?

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:10.160
The coins are always in your hand.

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:12.110
In my hand?

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.890
It's changing color!

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.320
I told you.

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:21.500
The time you've been given has a limit.

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:24.400
By tomorrow morning, it will change to black,

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:25.660
and you will disappear.

00:14:27.690 --> 00:14:29.870
Why? That's not...

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.680
Disappear... What does that mean?

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.890
What happens to me?

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:38.420
As time passes, your memories will fade,

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.400
your memories will be devoured,

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:44.900
and everything within you

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:46.150
will disappear.

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:50.450
Chi-chan...

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:52.430
No...

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:54.400
I don't want to forget.

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:55.660
Hello.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:58.790
You're a Selector, aren't you?

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.980
Don't be so scared.

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:03.310
I am, too.

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:07.660
This all suddenly kind of happened.

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:09.220
I don't know what to do.

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:13.370
It looks like we can't avoid fighting forever.

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.080
Sorry that I'm just a beginner,

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:17.500
but would you battle me?

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:21.810
Suzuko, this is your last chance.

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:26.320
When you want to start a battle, 
hold up your card and shout, "Open."

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:29.000
The card will guide you the rest of the way.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:31.480
Suzu!

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:36.980
I...

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:39.040
I don't want to forget.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:41.870
Open!

00:15:58.470 --> 00:15:59.820
What is this place?

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:01.230
The battle field.

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:04.270
Where Selector battles are held.

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:06.020
The battle field?

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.320
Bingo!

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:09.300
I figured you wouldn't know anything.

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:11.730
And you just have one coin left.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:13.220
I have four.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:15.860
Okay, I'm just gonna stomp you.

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:17.280
Don't blame me.

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:21.720
Aiming for weak-looking targets 
is the way to win.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.440
Suzuko will have the first turn.

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:32.600
The first turn?

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:33.400
U-Um—

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:34.440
Calm down.

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:36.920
Grow me first.

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:38.970
O-Okay.

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:39.640
Grow!

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.050
Um, next...

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:47.650
You're so slow!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.380
Stop taking so long.

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:51.110
If you're done, you say, "Turn end"!

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:53.010
This is the problem with beginners.

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.590
T-Turn end!

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:55.780
Suzuko!

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:00.020
You seriously ended your turn!

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:02.310
Sure you don't want any weapons at all?

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:04.080
U-Um...

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:09.140
Bullying a beginner like this is kind of mean.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:10.530
Shut up, Slow-ko!

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:11.210
I'm sorry!

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.070
Grow, Slow-ass!

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:13.470
Right!

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:17.590
Place the SIGNI, and attack with full force!

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:18.720
Okay.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:45.380
Riru!

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.830
Don't worry.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.450
It's your turn, Suzuko.

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:50.130
What do I do?

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:55.470
Ensuring your formation balances attack 
and defense is the most important thing.

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:58.340
First, grow me, and then summon your SIGNI.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:17:59.860
G-Got it.

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:01.050
Grow!

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:05.480
And then summon Valor Gawain,

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.100
and do a full attack!

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:14.270
Not bad.

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:16.260
Slow-ko, summon Otedama!

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:17.630
O-Okay.

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:18.700
Attack!

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:21.950
Riru, attack with a Servant!

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:35.380
<i>So this is a Selector Battle.</i>

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:49.560
I'm sorry!

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:51.770
Riru!

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.050
Riru?

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:59.200
It isn't over yet...

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:01.870
It's impossible.

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:05.460
I... I can't do it!

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:07.130
I'm going to lose!

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:09.050
Chi-chan...

00:19:09.050 --> 00:19:12.040
Come on, attack already.

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:14.250
No matter what you do, it won't matter.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:17.970
I have an impregnable Defensive ARTS.

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:20.820
Any damage I take will charge my ener,

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:24.760
and I'll beat the crap out of your little 
Riru with some really nasty ARTS!

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:26.900
Defensive ARTS...

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:29.300
Then, even if I attack...

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:30.940
Suzu, hang in there.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:36.020
Suzu, hang in there!

00:19:39.930 --> 00:19:44.800
<i>He's only gone after beginners like me.</i>

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:47.040
<i>He looks down on them, 
underestimates them.</i>

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:51.250
<i>He doesn't think about 
strengthening his defense.</i>

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:54.960
<i>But if what he says is true, Riru will...</i>

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.380
Suzuko...

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:58.300
Bet your coin.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:19:58.880
My coin?

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:03.380
You don't fight your battles alone.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:07.160
Bet everything you have on me.

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:19.490
Coin bet!

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:26.340
Honest!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.540
Honest? Like an honest person?

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.540
That looks like a coin skill.

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:36.690
Idiot.

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:38.960
Listen, that stuff about 
Defensive ARTS was a lie.

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:41.670
Of course I don't have anything like that.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:45.130
Once I attack again, it'll be over.

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:47.630
That's the problem with beginners.

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:48.300
Why am I—

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:51.180
Riru, go!

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:04.570
Damn it all!

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:08.160
How could I lose to such a beginner?

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:11.000
Listen, this won't happen next time!

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:14.210
Congratulations.

00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:17.210
Now you have two coins left.

00:21:17.620 --> 00:21:18.540
Yeah.

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:20.590
Suzu, hang in there.

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:23.240
Riru, you're kind of...

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:24.440
Like Chinatsu?

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:28.580
I was made from your memories.

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:30.510
If I am like Chinatsu,

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:35.790
that just shows how important 
Chinatsu is inside you.

00:21:37.680 --> 00:21:39.550
I see...

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:42.400
So Chi-chan is inside me.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.660
Welcome, Selector.

00:23:26.950 --> 00:23:28.100
This is just a game.

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:29.650
I want it over with.

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:30.740
You're a Selector, right?

00:23:30.740 --> 00:23:31.950
Disappear? What will?

00:23:31.950 --> 00:23:33.060
You just have to win.

00:23:33.060 --> 00:23:34.800
You only have one coin, huh?

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:35.970
You will not use your coin?

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:37.820
I won't lose.

00:23:37.820 --> 00:23:40.980
Next time: Girl / Ideal and Reality.

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:40.980
Girl / Ideal and Reality
